# .cursorrules (Detailed Constitution / Mirror Notes)

## 0) Auto-Synced Normative Block (Read-Only, Source: `AGENTS.md`)
<!-- SYNC_BLOCK_START -->
Priority: system/dev/runtime > user > AGENTS.md > .cursorrules
Session Gate: read PROJECT_STATUS.md -> 2-line current-focus summary -> declare mode
Mode: compact by default; precision on high-risk triggers; keep precision through validation
Precision triggers: files>=5, StepData change, serialization change, thread/signal change, runner flow change, unclear repro/scope
Multi-Agent flow: default Executor->Guardian; precision trigger -> Planner->Executor->Guardian
Role constraints: Planner no code edits; Guardian read-only PASS/FAIL gate
Governance: rule-file changes (AGENTS/.cursorrules/rule-guard tests) in dedicated change set
Constitutional files: AGENTS.md, .cursorrules, tests/test_rule_docs_sync.py, tests/test_rule_guard_steps_mutation.py
Constitutional policy: no delete/recreate; edit+diff only; isolated change set
Risk snapshot: create pre-refactor commit for runner/signal/StepData
Session close: status clean + intended diff + required tests green
Thread/UI safety: worker threads never touch UI directly; use pyqtSignal
State ownership: MainWindow owns steps/UndoStack; dialogs return data only
Command rule: no direct self.steps CRUD/reorder; use _push_command(...)
Data integrity: StepData changes require model+serialization+runner+tests; defaults backward-safe
Quality gate: focused tests for core; full pytest for risky changes; health_check for runtime-sensitive
Mutation guard: keep tests/test_rule_guard_steps_mutation.py passing
Sync guard: keep tests/test_rule_docs_sync.py passing
Docs sync: DEV_LOG.md + PROJECT_STATUS.md + now_spec.md on meaningful behavior changes
Environment: do not modify backups/
Sync policy: AGENTS.md canonical; .cursorrules mirrors this block only; direction AGENTS -> .cursorrules
<!-- SYNC_BLOCK_END -->

## 1) Detailed Mode Guidance
### 1.1 Compact Mode
- Use for low/medium tasks:
  - docs edits
  - small focused bug fixes
  - routine test updates
- Keep context reads minimal.
- Report only deltas.

### 1.2 Precision Mode
- Use for high-risk/high-complexity tasks:
  - multi-module refactor
  - thread/signal changes
  - data model/schema changes
  - runtime orchestration
  - unclear root cause regressions
- Expand assumptions/risks/verification scope.
- Do not exit precision until risk is retired.

## 2) Session Start Checklist (Operational)
1. Open `PROJECT_STATUS.md` first.
2. Extract current focus (or nearest equivalent) and summarize in 2 lines.
3. Declare `Compact`/`Precision` before changing files.
4. If repro is missing, ask for repro or run conservative precision checks.

## 3) Multi-Agent Operations (Detailed)
### 3.1 Default (2-Agent)
1. `Executor` implements with minimal diff.
2. `Guardian` performs read-only review and decides PASS/FAIL.

### 3.2 Escalated (3-Agent)
1. `Planner` prepares plan/risk/verification/rollback only.
2. `Executor` implements Planner scope.
3. `Guardian` reviews and gates release.

### 3.3 Escalation Trigger
- Any precision trigger immediately upgrades to 3-Agent flow.

### 3.4 Role Rules
- Planner:
  - No code changes.
  - Must declare mode and risk-driven test plan.
- Executor:
  - No architecture drift beyond approved plan.
  - Must run targeted tests first, then full pytest if risky.
- Guardian:
  - Read-only.
  - Must include exact file/line failures when FAIL.

### 3.5 Prompt Templates
- Use `MULTI_AGENT_PROTOCOL.md` for copy/paste Planner/Executor/Guardian templates.

## 4) Architecture Iron Rules (Expanded)
1. Thread safety:
   - `MacroRunner`/`TriggerWatcher` never update UI directly.
   - Route UI changes via `pyqtSignal` + main-thread slots.
2. Single source of truth:
   - `MainWindow` owns `steps` + `UndoStack`.
   - Dialogs pass data back only.
3. Command pattern enforcement:
   - Use command objects + `self._push_command(...)` for CRUD/reorder.
   - Avoid ad-hoc list mutation paths.
4. Branch stability:
   - Prefer `step_id` over index.
   - Missing target must fail-safe.

## 5) Token Efficiency Protocol
1. Delta-first reporting only.
2. Short progress updates.
3. Avoid repeated checklist text in one turn.
4. Run targeted tests first; full suite only when risk requires.
5. Keep external consultation prompts compact (`CONSULT_TOKEN_TEMPLATE.md`).

## 6) UI/Regression Guard
1. Hide-all then show-needed for dynamic groups.
2. Keep `layout.addWidget(...)` paths intact.
3. Run visibility/state refresh after init/load.

## 7) Data/Runtime Integrity
1. `StepData` field change requires synchronized updates:
   - model
   - load/save/serialization
   - runner usage
   - tests
2. Preserve backward compatibility by default.
3. No partial production logic edits.

## 8) Quality Gate (Expanded)
1. Core changes: focused tests immediately.
2. Risky/cross-cutting: `python -m pytest -q`.
3. Runtime-sensitive: `python run_health_check.py` when applicable.
4. Guard tests must stay green:
   - `tests/test_rule_guard_steps_mutation.py`
   - `tests/test_rule_docs_sync.py`

## 9) Documentation Sync
- For meaningful behavior changes, update:
  - `DEV_LOG.md`
  - `PROJECT_STATUS.md`
  - `now_spec.md`
- Include latest pass counts when changed.

## 10) Environment Notes
- Workspace root: `d:\down\autocording\매크로모듈화`
- CMD quoting can be brittle; prefer small commands and minimal pattern complexity.
- Never modify `backups/`.

## 11) Git Governance (Detailed)
1. Local repository must stay Git-tracked.
2. Before edits:
   - `git status`
   - `git diff`
3. Constitutional files:
   - `AGENTS.md`
   - `.cursorrules`
   - `tests/test_rule_docs_sync.py`
   - `tests/test_rule_guard_steps_mutation.py`
4. Constitutional file edits:
   - Never delete/recreate.
   - Edit-in-place and verify diff.
   - Keep as dedicated change set, never mixed with feature work.
5. Before risky refactor (`runner/signal/StepData`):
   - Create snapshot commit first.
6. Recovery commands are allowed with explicit intent:
   - `git log --oneline`
   - `git checkout <commit_id>`
   - `git reset --hard <commit_id>`

## 12) Sync/Conflict Policy
1. Canonical source: `AGENTS.md`.
2. Mirror scope in this file:
   - Only the block between `SYNC_BLOCK_START/END`.
3. Sync direction:
   - `AGENTS.md` -> `.cursorrules` only.
4. Do not back-write `AGENTS.md` from `.cursorrules`.
5. If mismatch exists:
   - Treat `AGENTS.md` as authoritative and resync mirror block.
